{
  "dom_id": "step-q147523",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/assets/771f1ffeda2b0041e1485611315661eed0bc88a601513d4fd4b2088022521aa8.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-2,2)$, $(1,-1)$,  and $(-2,2).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/assets/e1faae8b1750b1c402f88ef801cd6609d259c37c523ac4bf4a7cb795034a9bd1.png)",
